# Line endings are part of the content here, not a checkout preference. Committed artifacts
# (catalog.json, the v2 schema, the rules-output digests) are compared byte-for-byte against a
# string built in memory with LF, and raw string literals in .cs carry the source file's endings
# into the assertions that search them. A CRLF checkout fails those tests without anything being
# wrong. See #44.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touched. Git's heuristic would get these right anyway; saying so removes the question.
*.dem binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.tris binary
